      "side": 1,
      "message": "No. MctpRequester sends one request at a time per EID (handleResult() in MctpRequester.cpp). A GET that lands before the SET completes sees awaitingReadback still false; one that lands after was sent after the SET completed, so it already reads the new thresholds. SETs cannot overlap. Added ReadingBeforeTheSetLandsKeepsTheGateShut to cover this.",
